# The base carries a fractured spell suppression roll, so every reforge keeps
# it. Deafening Essence of Greed guarantees life and is repeated until one
# elemental resistance lands at tier 1 (a Harvest swap can move it to the
# right element later). With the Eater dominant, an Eldritch Orb of Annulment
# only ever removes a suffix, which is how the craft opens a suffix slot
# without risking the life roll; losing the resistance sends the craft back to
# the essences. The implicits come last: embers until the Exarch one is the
# strike one, then Orbs of Conflict until it is Exquisite. A Conflict may
# raise either side and lowers the other, and a lowered Lesser implicit drops
# off: the Lesser Eater an ichor puts back goes each time the Exarch rises, and
# the Exarch itself can fall away, when the embers start again.

item {
    base:     "Dragonscale Gauntlets"
    ilvl:     86
    rarity:   rare
    suffixes: [ fractured "suppress spell damage" t2 ]
}

def anyEleRes(t) =
    has "fire resistance" t
    or has "cold resistance" t
    or has "lightning resistance" t

until anyEleRes(t1) and suffixCount <= 2 {
    until anyEleRes(t1) {
        essence "greed" t1
    }

    # Make room on the suffix side under Eater dominance; the fractured mod
    # and the prefixes are safe from an eldritch annul there.
    if suffixCount == 3 {
        ichor lesser
        eldritch annul
    }
}

bench "fire and chaos resistance"

# Implicits: the strike Exarch implicit, raised to Exquisite.
until exarch exquisite "strike skills target" {
    until exarch "strike skills target" {
        ember grand
    }
    if not eater {
        ichor lesser
    }
    conflict
}
